        "original_id": "9bc68bfe-3b21-55d3-b14d-c5d4fe72bd12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Philadelphus, Sarracenia\n- Concepts: plant genera, species counts, native ranges, common names\n\nFacts:\n- Philadelphus is a genus of about 60 species of shrubs that grow 3 to 20 feet (1 to 6 meters) tall.\n- Philadelphus is commonly called mock-orange and is native to North America, Central America, Asia, and locally in southeast Europe.\n- Sarracenia is a North American genus of pitcher plants comprising 8 to 11 species.\n- Sarracenia is commonly called trumpet pitchers.",
